==Finnish==

===Etymology===
Causative aspect of the verb {{term|juoda||to drink}}; {{suffix||alt1=juo-|ttaa|lang=fi}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|juot|taa|lang=fi}}
* {{rhymes|lang=fi|uotːɑː}}
* {{IPA|lang=fi|/ˈjuɔtːɑːˣ/}}

===Verb===
{{fi-verb|cat=causative}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=fi}} To [[give]] someone something to [[drink]]; to [[water]] (an animal); to [[make]] someone drink, to be [[pushy]] in [[offer]]ing something to drink, (often) to get [[drunk]].
#: '''''Juotin''' [[lapsi|lapselle]] [[vesi|vettä]].''
#:: ''I '''gave''' the kid water '''to drink'''.'' / ''I '''made''' the child '''drink''' some water.''
#: '''''Juotin''' [[koira]]a.'' / '''''Juotin''' [[koira]]n.'' / '''''Juotin''' [[koira]]lle [[vesi|vettä]].''
#:: ''I '''watered''' the dog.''
# To use milk to [[fatten]], [[feed]] young animals meant for [[slaughter]].
# {{context|transitive|lang=fi}} To [[solder]].

